{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793640378,"nonce":"GM2yrN1mUTrY5NLdlfEqfxuifWY=","title":"Antialias tessellated paths without MSAA: feathered strokes and fringe fills","message":"Paths rely on MSAA, which costs a 4x target and a resolve per batch and is absent on 1x targets (the web default). Cheaper analytic coverage:\n\n- Strokes: the tessellator already computes each vertex's distance to the stroke edge (path.rs, half_width - dist_from_center). Widen the stroke by half a pixel and smoothstep that distance (with fwidth) in path.wgsl.\n- Fills: emit a ~1px fringe strip along the outline with alpha 1 -\u003e 0 outward and leave the interior opaque (the NanoVG / Skia approach). The disabled attempt in path.wgsl put an edge distance on the fill triangles themselves, whose vertices all lie on the outline, so every pixel read as on the edge and faded.\n\nSdfBuilder::line now draws a capsule as a rotated rounded rect; arc, quad_bezier and the booleans are still stubs in paint/sdf_builder.rs.","files":null}]}